The framework positions the UAE as a regional leader in sustainable finance, contributing to global efforts in achieving the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).', 'UAE', 'climate', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Arab Emirates', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/183_19', ARRAY['sdg4', 'sdg13', 'sdg7', 'sdg17', 'uae', 'voluntary', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9', 'voluntary_frameworks']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('4142036d-a031-583d-b042-da8c6cd9d450', 'UAE DFM''s Guide to ESG Reporting', 'DFM''s Guide to ESG Reporting, 2023', 'In line with its commitment to drive market growth and sustainability in financial markets, Dubai Financial Market (DFM) has introduced this Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Guide to introduce issuers to the general global ESG reporting frameworks and assist them in navigating the ESG reporting landscape with relevant information to investors.', 'In line with its commitment to drive market growth and sustainability in financial markets, Dubai Financial Market (DFM) has introduced this Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Guide to introduce issuers to the general global ESG reporting frameworks and assist them in navigating the ESG reporting landscape with relevant information to investors.', 'In line with its commitment to drive market growth and sustainability in financial markets, Dubai Financial Market (DFM) has introduced this Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Guide to introduce issuers to the general global ESG reporting frameworks and assist them in navigating the ESG reporting landscape with relevant information to investors.', 'UAE', 'climate', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Arab Emirates', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/183_22', ARRAY['mandatory', 'uae', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('59106758-7f11-50b2-a87b-844cf4e5ae5b', 'UAE Companies Regulations (Amendment )', 'Companies Regulations (Amendment No. 2)', 'The Companies Regulations (Amendment No. 2), 2023, introduces mandatory Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) disclosure requirements for in-scope companies under Chapter 4A of the Abu Dhabi Global Market (ADGM) Companies Regulations. This amendment aligns corporate reporting practices with international ESG standards, supporting the UAE’s commitment to achieving net-zero emissions by 2050. The regulation adopts a "comply or explain" approach and defines threshold conditions for mandatory compliance.

Key provisions include:

Threshold Conditions:

Companies with annual turnover exceeding USD 68 million.

FSRA-licensed financial institutions managing assets above USD 6 billion.

Mandatory ESG Disclosures:

In-scope companies must disclose ESG-related performance, development, and strategy based on recognized international frameworks (e.g., GRI, CDP, ISSB).

Exemptions apply to subsidiaries included in group disclosures and certain listed or restricted scope companies.

Governance and Accountability:

Companies may provide written explanations for non-compliance.

ESG disclosures must be included in annual reports or accompanying documents.

This regulation emphasizes transparency, consistency, and alignment with global best practices, fostering responsible corporate behavior and enhancing investor confidence.', 'The Companies Regulations (Amendment No. 2), 2023, introduces mandatory Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) disclosure requirements for in-scope companies under Chapter 4A of the Abu Dhabi Global Market (ADGM) Companies Regulations. This amendment aligns corporate reporting practices with international ESG standards, supporting the UAE’s commitment to achieving net-zero emissions by 2050. The regulation adopts a "comply or explain" approach and defines threshold conditions for mandatory compliance.

Key provisions include:

