This framework enhances climate-related financial transparency in UK public sector reporting, supporting better policy alignment and risk mitigation.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_6', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'uk', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg6', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('84592de7-12b3-57f8-bdb2-88fbc2a3e9e9', 'UK Procurement Regulation', 'The Procurement Regulation 2024', 'The Procurement Regulation 2024 establishes rules for public procurement in the UK, covering transparency, publication of notices on a central digital platform, and defining key terms. It targets government officials, suppliers, and the public involved in procurement processes.', 'The Procurement Regulation 2024 establishes rules for public procurement in the UK, covering transparency, publication of notices on a central digital platform, and defining key terms. It targets government officials, suppliers, and the public involved in procurement processes.', 'The Procurement Regulation 2024 establishes rules for public procurement in the UK, covering transparency, publication of notices on a central digital platform, and defining key terms. It targets government officials, suppliers, and the public involved in procurement processes.', 'UK', 'circularity', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/185_113', ARRAY['uk', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('b29979b7-3591-5fba-8b8a-aa6efd450c04', 'UK Green Agreements Guidance: Guidance on the application', 'Green Agreements Guidance: Guidance on the application of the Chapter 1 prohibition in the Competition Act 1998 to environmental sustainability agreements', 'The UK''s "Green Agreements Guidance" clarifies competition rules for businesses partnering on sustainable initiatives. It highlights agreements unlikely to harm competition (e.g., sharing research on sustainable materials) and offers a flexible approach for climate change agreements. However, agreements restricting prices or sensitive information, while possible, require careful assessment to avoid potential antitrust issues.', 'The UK''s "Green Agreements Guidance" clarifies competition rules for businesses partnering on sustainable initiatives. It highlights agreements unlikely to harm competition (e.g., sharing research on sustainable materials) and offers a flexible approach for climate change agreements. However, agreements restricting prices or sensitive information, while possible, require careful assessment to avoid potential antitrust issues.', 'The UK''s "Green Agreements Guidance" clarifies competition rules for businesses partnering on sustainable initiatives. It highlights agreements unlikely to harm competition (e.g., sharing research on sustainable materials) and offers a flexible approach for climate change agreements. However, agreements restricting prices or sensitive information, while possible, require careful assessment to avoid potential antitrust issues.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_105', ARRAY['sdg13', 'sdg14', 'other sustainability policy', 'uk', 'regulations', 'mandatory']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('248495f7-40e5-5655-928e-9efc7cefff52', 'UK Commercial Organisations and Public Authorities Duty (Human Rights', 'Commercial Organisations and Public Authorities Duty (Human Rights and Environment) Bill [HL]', 'A bill to place a duty on commercial organisations and public authorities to prevent human rights and environmental harms, including an obligation to conduct and publish human rights and environmental due diligence assessments, on their own operations, subsidiaries, and value chains; to make provision for civil liability, penalties, and a criminal offence for failures to comply with the duty; and for connected purposes.', 'A bill to place a duty on commercial organisations and public authorities to prevent human rights and environmental harms, including an obligation to conduct and publish human rights and environmental due diligence assessments, on their own operations, subsidiaries, and value chains; to make provision for civil liability, penalties, and a criminal offence for failures to comply with the duty; and for connected purposes.', 'A bill to place a duty on commercial organisations and public authorities to prevent human rights and environmental harms, including an obligation to conduct and publish human rights and environmental due diligence assessments, on their own operations, subsidiaries, and value chains; to make provision for civil liability, penalties, and a criminal offence for failures to comply with the duty; and for connected purposes.', 'UK', 'governance', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_107', ARRAY['uk', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d2f02b5c-279c-5af2-932a-c6446a335386', 'UK PS23/16: Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) and investment labels', 'PS23/16: Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) and investment labels', 'This Policy Statement (PS) contains our final rules and guidance to improve trust and transparency to the market for sustainable investment products. It follows our consultation on Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) and investment labels (CP22/20), issued in October 2022.', 'This Policy Statement (PS) contains our final rules and guidance to improve trust and transparency to the market for sustainable investment products. It follows our consultation on Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) and investment labels (CP22/20), issued in October 2022.', 'This Policy Statement (PS) contains our final rules and guidance to improve trust and transparency to the market for sustainable investment products. It follows our consultation on Sustainability Disclosure Requirements (SDR) and investment labels (CP22/20), issued in October 2022.', 'UK', 'governance', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_108', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'uk', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('5c9a744c-98dc-5f4b-8fa9-f149ce5c1214', 'UK Sustainability Reporting Guidance', 'Sustainability Reporting Guidance: 2023-24', 'This document sets out the principles and standards underpinning sustainability reporting for use in central government. This report outlines the minimum statutory reporting requirements, some best practice examples, and underlying principles to be adopted. The guidance is applicable to all central government bodies that fall within the scope of the Greening Government Commitments (GGCs), and which produce annual reports and accounts in accordance with the Government Financial Reporting Manual (FReM)', 'This document sets out the principles and standards underpinning sustainability reporting for use in central government. This report outlines the minimum statutory reporting requirements, some best practice examples, and underlying principles to be adopted. The guidance is applicable to all central government bodies that fall within the scope of the Greening Government Commitments (GGCs), and which produce annual reports and accounts in accordance with the Government Financial Reporting Manual (FReM)', 'This document sets out the principles and standards underpinning sustainability reporting for use in central government. This report outlines the minimum statutory reporting requirements, some best practice examples, and underlying principles to be adopted. The guidance is applicable to all central government bodies that fall within the scope of the Greening Government Commitments (GGCs), and which produce annual reports and accounts in accordance with the Government Financial Reporting Manual (FReM)', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_109', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'uk', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('805fb6d7-b8cc-5fe5-9ed9-5b27d408ecfa', 'UK Procurement Act', 'Procurement Act 2023', 'The Procurement Act 2023 in the United Kingdom defines procurement terms, contracting authorities, and excluded entities. It outlines procedures for awarding and managing contracts, targeting contracting authorities and entities involved in public contracts.', 'The Procurement Act 2023 in the United Kingdom defines procurement terms, contracting authorities, and excluded entities. It outlines procedures for awarding and managing contracts, targeting contracting authorities and entities involved in public contracts.', 'The Procurement Act 2023 in the United Kingdom defines procurement terms, contracting authorities, and excluded entities. It outlines procedures for awarding and managing contracts, targeting contracting authorities and entities involved in public contracts.', 'UK', 'circularity', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/185_112', ARRAY['mandatory', 'uk', 'sdg12', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
